  "id": "secondskin",
  "note": "SECOND SKIN, the clothes shop on Cinder Lane. The tile's prose: a narrow shopfront with its whole stock argument in the window, three mannequins staged so the good coat is at the back, and the glass is clean, which on Cinder Lane is a statement.\n\nSo it is a narrow two-storey shop in buff stock brick with a flat over it, the terrace this end of the lane is built of: one wide clean window with two mullions (three panes, three mannequins), the door to one side, a dark green fascia with the name on it, and three sashes upstairs. A single-storey passage wing beside it keeps it narrow on a full tile, and a back extension and a chimney give it a roofline from the air.\n\nIt replaced a mauve stack of cantilevered boxes with a chamfered crown, which was the same template as the Cherry Pit and Dead Space Interiors beside it and made the three read as one strip mall. No neon: a clothes shop gets a lit window and a painted board, and the club next door gets the pink.",
  "pal": "ty_skel",
  "replaces": "boutique",
